      "id": 11,
      "title": "Implement Persistent Storage for VectorMemory using HNSW or SQLite",
      "description": "Enhance the VectorMemory module to support disk-based persistent storage of embeddings and metadata using either HNSW or SQLite, while maintaining the existing API and ensuring efficient similarity search capabilities.",
      "details": "Extend the VectorMemory module to store vector embeddings and associated metadata on disk rather than only in memory. This implementation should:\n\n1. Create a new storage backend that uses either:\n   - HNSW (Hierarchical Navigable Small World) for efficient approximate nearest neighbor search\n   - SQLite with appropriate indexing for vector similarity search\n\n2. Maintain the existing API methods:\n   - `addMemory(text, embedding, metadata)` - Should now persist to disk\n   - `querySimilar(embedding, limit)` - Should query from persistent storage\n\n3. Implement a configuration mechanism to specify storage location, index parameters, and other relevant settings\n\n4. Add a migration utility to transfer existing in-memory data to the new persistent storage\n\n5. Ensure thread-safety for concurrent read/write operations\n\n6. Implement proper resource management (connection pooling if using SQLite, index loading/unloading for HNSW)\n\n7. Add performance optimizations:\n   - Caching frequently accessed vectors\n   - Batch operations for bulk imports\n   - Background indexing for large datasets\n\n8. Handle edge cases:\n   - Graceful recovery from corrupted storage\n   - Automatic reindexing when needed\n   - Versioning for future compatibility\n\nDependencies to consider:\n- For HNSW: hnswlib, faiss, or similar libraries\n- For SQLite: sqlite3 with appropriate extensions for vector operations\n\nPerformance requirements:\n- Should support at least 1M vectors with sub-second query times\n- Minimal memory footprint regardless of dataset size",
      "testStrategy": "Testing should verify both functional correctness and performance characteristics:\n\n1. Unit Tests:\n   - Test persistence by adding vectors, restarting the service, and verifying they can be retrieved\n   - Verify that metadata is correctly stored and retrieved with vectors\n   - Test edge cases: empty database, very large vectors, malformed inputs\n   - Verify API compatibility with existing code that uses VectorMemory\n\n2. Integration Tests:\n   - Test the migration utility with various dataset sizes\n   - Verify that existing application flows work with the new storage backend\n\n3. Performance Tests:\n   - Benchmark query times for different dataset sizes (10K, 100K, 1M vectors)\n   - Measure memory usage during operation\n   - Test concurrent read/write operations and verify correctness\n   - Compare performance between HNSW and SQLite implementations\n\n4. Stress Tests:\n   - Test with very large datasets to verify scaling capabilities\n   - Simulate disk failures or corruption and verify recovery\n\n5. Specific Test Cases:\n   - Add 1000 vectors, restart, verify all are retrievable\n   - Perform similarity search and compare results with in-memory implementation\n   - Verify that updates to existing vectors are correctly persisted\n   - Test with various embedding dimensions (128, 384, 768, 1536)\n   - Verify that deleting vectors removes them from persistent storage",
      "status": "pending",
